"createdAt":"2020-07-01T10:29:35Z","entityUuid":"205a886d-83d7-4359-ae63-7103e05357c3","parentUuid":"4e0c1edf-660c-4ebf-81f5-9fa959dead30","uuid":"904f79bd-a156-4b54-8956-f6c9637b0826"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"Not applicable: none of the data is personal data"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-07-01T10:29:36Z","entityUuid":"19ee5b2f-4ed2-4508-9265-9773229dcc36","parentUuid":"467ff3ad-156c-4285-9efb-c91072b3544e","uuid":"bad76bd8-1699-480c-b210-662e5ec02783"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditChapterEvent","questionUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["73d686bd-7939-412e-8631-502ee6d9ea7b","c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","83c0d09d-e74c-4c81-a52c-aaa2e18415ac","09c7c989-6461-417f-b09e-228491c051c6"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-07-01T10:29:37Z","entityUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","parentUuid":"6f6241d9-136c-4770-9d58-8a3f39607052","uuid":"f6371d27-baa3-49a3-9c65-f3e009ab2f29"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Project(s)"}},"createdAt":"2020-07-01T10:29:38Z","entityUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","parentUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","uuid":"d05b3565-3b7b-4c8e-835c-1e9d289c820e"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Contributors"}},"createdAt":"2020-07-01T10:29:39Z","entityUuid":"73d686bd-7939-412e-8631-502ee6d9ea7b","parentUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","uuid":"65e3b050-8524-411e-8ff8-1a524583361d"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.2.0","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.1.0","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\n\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\n\n## Changelog\n\n### 2.2.0\n\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\n\n### 2.1.0\n\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\n\n### 2.0.2\n\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\n\n### 2.0.1\n\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\n\n### 2.0.0\n\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\n* Added administrative chapter\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\n\n### 1.4.0\n\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\n\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\n\n### 1.3.0\n\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\n\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\n\n### 1.2.0\n\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\n\n### 1.1.0\n\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\n\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*. \n\n### 1.0.3\n\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\n\n### 1.0.2\n\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\n\n### 1.0.1\n\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\n\n### 1.0.0\n\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.2.0"},{"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:19.845Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditChapterEvent","questionUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["efc80cc8-8318-4f8c-acb7-dc1c60e491c1"]},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Before you decide to embark on any new study, it is good practice to check all options to re-use existing available data, either collected or generated by yourself in an earlier project, or data from others (Barend Mons calls this \"Other PEople's Data And Services\" or OPEDAS). This can include reusable data that have been created for an earlier study, and also so-called \"reference data\" which is used by many projects.\n\nIt is not because we can generate massive amounts of data that we always need to do so. Creating data with public money is bringing with it the responsibility to treat those data well and (if potentially useful) make them available for re-use by others. And the circle is only complete if such data is actually re-used."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:20Z","entityUuid":"82fd0cce-2b41-423f-92ad-636d0872045c","parentUuid":"6f6241d9-136c-4770-9d58-8a3f39607052","uuid":"6e0372d1-d20b-4a55-b278-8f6bf574517e"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"It is possible that you have overlooked existing data! This question is not only about data sets that are similar to what you want to determine yourself, but also reference data or data that should be mined from the existing literature. Further, it is very likely that you will refer to related data, e.g. other databases where you usually \"quickly look something up\", but that could maybe be properly integrated, especially if you need to do such lookups multiple times."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:21Z","entityUuid":"72cdbc99-2707-4817-ac40-435a03e5e837","parentUuid":"efc80cc8-8318-4f8c-acb7-dc1c60e491c1","uuid":"66b4d227-7082-4bc7-9159-491c9bde1f61"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Many research fields have worked together to define what kind of metadata should really be collected when an experiment of a certain kind is performed and described. That information is described in a Minimal Metadata Standard. Often, these standards describe both what kind of information needs to be collected as well as the format in which it is expected."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:22Z","entityUuid":"6226d7f2-565f-4991-94b3-c00be6aca20e","parentUuid":"6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb","uuid":"97a747cb-0655-460d-830c-e311669cda8b"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Have you identified types of data that you will use that are used by others too? Some types of data (for example \"images\" or \"tables\") are used by many different projects. For such data, often common standards exist (in our example \"JPG\" and \"CSV\") that help to make these data reusable. Are you using such common data formats?\n\nPlease make sure you list all the data types that are important for your project. You should make sure also to list the formats used in any data sets that you are re-using."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:23Z","entityUuid":"b08fe063-33f8-4380-b3a9-ba1e586dedf2","parentUuid":"b1df3c74-0b1f-4574-81c4-4cc2d780c1af","uuid":"cce5bd15-cccc-4036-b6dd-1f410c79ec23"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":"Formats like XLS or SQL are very flexible; they can be adapted to many different uses, and this makes them good for interoperability. However, their flexibility also makes that it is not immediately obvious from the file structure how it can be used. The data needs a proper *description* in order for others (or yourself at a later time) to be able to unambiguously understand what it contains.","title":"Is this data format completely described?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:24Z","entityUuid":"192fc5d3-dc2a-495c-8f24-f59a4c5d95c9","parentUuid":"b08fe063-33f8-4380-b3a9-ba1e586dedf2","uuid":"fa5c4f5e-6570-4b30-8ba6-1e66edd1434e"},{"content":{"advice":"Plan time and budget for either documenting this data or for conversion to a well-described specific format.","annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:25Z","entityUuid":"14503afc-3fe3-4e28-8f2d-81c065ee7565","parentUuid":"192fc5d3-dc2a-495c-8f24-f59a4c5d95c9","uuid":"fba7bf6d-160c-4e1e-8629-2a944e0bb167"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:26Z","entityUuid":"d75d94bb-6c3a-4170-a5a1-2a75a78629c2","parentUuid":"192fc5d3-dc2a-495c-8f24-f59a4c5d95c9","uuid":"34d35098-d99d-47d5-b6cb-877e9249edfa"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Add each of the research project(s) that are you will be working on and for which the data and work are described in this DMP. Give each project a small identifying name for yourself."},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Research Project(s)"}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:27Z","entityUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","parentUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","uuid":"8c131c22-9ced-4684-b308-c77138382584"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"integrationUuid":{"changed":false},"questionType":"IntegrationQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Give the name of the database or dataset. You will be shown suggestions of data bases from FAIRSharing, but you can also type the name of a dataset that is not in FAIRsharing"},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Reference database or dataset"},"variables":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:28Z","entityUuid":"93988527-5bff-4125-8834-3750e9a28683","parentUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","uuid":"cefc363b-d458-4632-9ca9-986efb9e3561"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Specify a URL or a persistent identifier (e.g. DOI) for the database or dataset."},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Where is this data available"},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:29Z","entityUuid":"7801fe70-a2ac-432b-9470-e326646c249f","parentUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","uuid":"b77198d5-7932-45f8-8b68-cb5302109105"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"What are the conditions of use for this database or dataset?"}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:30Z","entityUuid":"aee03da5-b399-4274-8db4-fac82c6210d3","parentUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","uuid":"a90aa561-1cd4-43ed-8315-e9ba0bc7fd0f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Many reference datasets and databases evolve over time. If the reference data changes, this may affect your results. If different versions of a reference data exist, you need to establish your \"version policy\"."},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Is the reference database or dataset versioned?"}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:31Z","entityUuid":"10b6548c-21cd-44c8-a8de-47415e7b012e","parentUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","uuid":"077703f7-8e29-4c9c-b62b-03605e583e44"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Who else could be interested in using this data?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:32Z","entityUuid":"135aa977-ecc2-4bb8-aa55-2def9d9d6040","parentUuid":"f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc","uuid":"bc06630f-35cf-4bed-bb6b-dc17aa42e8b1"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Just us","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:33Z","entityUuid":"f5a4d36c-4ce8-4ab6-8e5e-d7a2418c77c7","parentUuid":"135aa977-ecc2-4bb8-aa55-2def9d9d6040","uuid":"561bd562-a4ac-4d72-9812-c834695aa320"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Other researchers working in the same field of research","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:34Z","entityUuid":"515cac06-d101-4af1-95ef-33fd6a2da8b0","parentUuid":"135aa977-ecc2-4bb8-aa55-2def9d9d6040","uuid":"251193b2-51d5-4c58-9ab8-7767250d7dd6"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Researchers working in other fields","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:35Z","entityUuid":"9270c716-f997-43e1-bc2a-55687e149dbd","parentUuid":"135aa977-ecc2-4bb8-aa55-2def9d9d6040","uuid":"93147f8b-2a2f-49c5-b6cb-d9aedc5edea7"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"How do you think other researchers can use this data?","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:36Z","entityUuid":"1ca28160-8b73-48fe-8b74-18c0f5cb56df","parentUuid":"9270c716-f997-43e1-bc2a-55687e149dbd","uuid":"8bf43c2d-a24f-4214-b0bc-b82bf3b4d0c5"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Who else could be interested in using this data?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:37Z","entityUuid":"c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1","parentUuid":"b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa","uuid":"3cb7b0cf-de34-474d-8984-fb372f421809"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Just us","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:38Z","entityUuid":"e862d2cb-967d-4f3b-b845-403259c79751","parentUuid":"c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1","uuid":"0e72130b-07aa-471e-8ef4-3c84ad350024"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Other researchers working in the same field of research","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:39Z","entityUuid":"1566d3af-666b-456a-9ace-daee8d690d6e","parentUuid":"c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1","uuid":"6129203e-d957-43ce-bd00-52475417e465"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Researchers working in other fields","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:40Z","entityUuid":"0c630b6f-8aec-4153-818d-90fbb559072f","parentUuid":"c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1","uuid":"6fac8b84-ce2f-4ecd-80fa-a307f6d2eeb4"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"How do you think other researchers can use this data?","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:41Z","entityUuid":"41a1b4ba-8cd5-47fe-a7be-06cccf9a1688","parentUuid":"0c630b6f-8aec-4153-818d-90fbb559072f","uuid":"dc00bbc1-9231-40bd-a767-9d58ae786009"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":true,"value":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e"},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:42Z","entityUuid":"c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1","parentUuid":"b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa","uuid":"4c32441d-e8ad-4e12-b484-0adf90d13ea1"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Project acronym","validations":[],"valueType":"StringQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:43Z","entityUuid":"5b765df9-299f-4855-9e99-aa844903f8f6","parentUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","uuid":"6c5da05f-4001-49de-b86b-8a17084f19e4"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["f0ef08fd-d733-465c-bc66-5de0b826c41b","5b765df9-299f-4855-9e99-aa844903f8f6","22583d74-3c98-4e0a-b363-26d767c88212","de84b9b5-bcd0-4954-8370-72ea83916b8c","cabc6f07-6015-454e-b97a-c34db4ec0c60","36a87eac-402d-43fb-a0df-ac5963bdf87d"]},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:44Z","entityUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","parentUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","uuid":"d1b4ebf1-6a23-4ea6-8d04-5cfa20332ddb"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"There are many kinds of metadata, each serving their own purpose.  Some key metadata that you should consider:\n* There is metadata that helps identify where the data is coming from (e.g. who created it, title). For this the Dublin Core is often used.\n* There are different ways of adding metadata to make the data \"discoverable\" for other researchers. This requires either keywords or ontology terms describing what is in the data.\n* There is metadata describing how the data can be re-used, such as license information and, for data about people, the extent of their consent for data reuse.\n* There is metadata describing where the data comes from and what it is useful for. For frequently used data types, there are often very well defined metadata standards, in other cases you may need to think about this yourself.\n"},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:45Z","entityUuid":"6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb","parentUuid":"8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3","uuid":"5ecdfeb7-dae1-47db-931c-24187afe136a"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"There are many kinds of metadata, each serving their own purpose.  Some key metadata that you should consider:\n* There is metadata that helps identify where the data is coming from (e.g. who created it, title). For this the Dublin Core is often used.\n* There are different ways of adding metadata to make the data \"discoverable\" for other researchers. This requires either keywords or ontology terms describing what is in the data.\n* There is metadata describing how the data can be re-used, such as license information and, for data about people, the extent of their consent for data reuse.\n* There is metadata that makes the data understandable, e.g. linking to the exact processes used to collect them (is a *body temperature* measured under the tongue or in the rectum?) and units (is a temperature given in Celsius or Fahrenheit?). \n* There is metadata describing where the data comes from and what it is useful for. For frequently used data types, there are often very well defined metadata standards, in other cases you may need to think about this yourself.\nFor each of these kinds of metadata there are specific standards. There is no single standard that will get you all the metadata needed to make the data as FAIR as possible.\n"},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:46Z","entityUuid":"6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb","parentUuid":"8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3","uuid":"413f05af-d68d-413e-bc14-0e299a67e05f"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"adc9133d-afcd-4616-9aea-db5f475898a2","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Will there be different versions of this data over time?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:47Z","entityUuid":"f99b1723-c8e4-44b9-af22-f66955eda1e2","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"bcd64d32-3ef1-41b4-914e-fd173fb9fe09"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:48Z","entityUuid":"41c0631f-c3d4-4c77-a293-ed0090f855e0","parentUuid":"f99b1723-c8e4-44b9-af22-f66955eda1e2","uuid":"6592f8fa-28be-4a22-8e0d-9430cfd2f6ea"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:49Z","entityUuid":"facde7e9-8711-4ced-a6f8-5fbacf929381","parentUuid":"f99b1723-c8e4-44b9-af22-f66955eda1e2","uuid":"69369d45-e554-4617-bb67-ef3f50aa8b64"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Will there be version numbers?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:50Z","entityUuid":"05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8","parentUuid":"facde7e9-8711-4ced-a6f8-5fbacf929381","uuid":"15b65ad2-f8f9-49c8-a42f-8f7d95ff5521"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"xx","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:51Z","entityUuid":"f069d137-35c7-4fb3-974a-ba69e40a77e3","parentUuid":"05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8","uuid":"356e3745-27b8-41d2-8c4d-d4dd83263786"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"How will the versions be recognised?"}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:52Z","entityUuid":"05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8","parentUuid":"facde7e9-8711-4ced-a6f8-5fbacf929381","uuid":"9e216751-be44-4e2a-80dc-a511f2aa4acc"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"They will be dated"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:53Z","entityUuid":"f069d137-35c7-4fb3-974a-ba69e40a77e3","parentUuid":"05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8","uuid":"2a7ac000-0866-45e7-92ee-bf9c41aca480"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"They will be clearly numbered","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:54Z","entityUuid":"283e382c-e200-4b19-b461-6c3c45334742","parentUuid":"05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8","uuid":"332e5e26-3046-4661-9464-bd488108af72"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Imagine yourself trying to interpret a similar data set from a colleague in a few years. \nIs there any way in which the data could be misinterpreted? Does everyone in the field do things in exactly the same way? And will that still be known in 10 years?\nHow can such misinterpretation be avoided?"},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:55Z","entityUuid":"44a9d6c0-f96c-47d2-8c7a-902a9c222067","parentUuid":"a23664b1-a17c-41fe-855c-db274984b355","uuid":"ea56edc6-ecca-4a13-99b5-50ac9d7fb7bf"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Has authority over the data been arranged for when the project is finished (potentially long after)?"}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:56Z","entityUuid":"feb954c1-c38e-4615-addd-4c714a06809a","parentUuid":"d748ea2b-bbe7-4b05-82e2-bee5e10e8441","uuid":"075ae527-9963-40b7-835e-d9333abebc1b"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":true,"value":"Through a Data Access Committee"},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:57Z","entityUuid":"f68a6141-3f78-4efb-8a80-2a482e75a862","parentUuid":"f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274","uuid":"b0f03c0c-f053-4271-a927-93c758a5fd59"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Consider that users of a data set will need to be able to get access several years after the project is finished. The best way to arrange this is to put the responsibility for checking the rights to access the data with a fixed body in an organisation, a data access committee, rather than one of the investigators of the project"},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:58Z","entityUuid":"f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274","parentUuid":"734d5f4e-91c0-4019-8164-8c70c2e0c8f2","uuid":"64e2afe1-50ae-438e-96c3-334b9b135f9c"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Consider what will happen if the contact person moves jobs."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:49:59Z","entityUuid":"15e7beff-1d71-4515-9517-26e222e672e5","parentUuid":"f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274","uuid":"7931bf5d-186f-4a68-a216-8da88e072c10"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Consider that users of a data set will need to be able to get access several years after the project is finished. The best way to arrange this is to put the responsibility for checking the rights to access the data with a fixed body in an organisation, a data access committee, rather than one of the investigators of the project."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:00Z","entityUuid":"f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274","parentUuid":"734d5f4e-91c0-4019-8164-8c70c2e0c8f2","uuid":"927db844-fa43-4902-817d-8f2fcc462871"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Please summarise the restrictions. Note that it is a good idea to publish the final conditions for use of the data openly, so that interested researchers can know beforehand whether they will be able to get access to the data before actually placing a request."},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:01Z","entityUuid":"30426255-b153-4f3e-bf20-f13573160a64","parentUuid":"734d5f4e-91c0-4019-8164-8c70c2e0c8f2","uuid":"2c8e16e4-495c-4c58-b66a-16904f844a8f"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Will a user of this data need specific software to be able to use it?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:02Z","entityUuid":"1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"8ad40baf-4d58-4dcb-9ee5-cd4615272530"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:03Z","entityUuid":"5d7aa34b-2e26-485a-be2b-5de39f788c3e","parentUuid":"1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a","uuid":"c2b9feeb-63d7-4388-b132-93cbe17573c3"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":true,"value":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e"},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:04Z","entityUuid":"1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"d06cc816-7fd7-49df-a92c-a00b557f4db5"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:05Z","entityUuid":"371461b3-3758-443d-b06a-fa37514be4da","parentUuid":"1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a","uuid":"dbadf1e9-6667-4a00-993d-04f86e53d6f8"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ListQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"What software is needed to use the data?"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:06Z","entityUuid":"b8543a67-2a6b-4f45-a0b0-d245227f9818","parentUuid":"371461b3-3758-443d-b06a-fa37514be4da","uuid":"67709376-954f-423f-8c01-8548455d5a0f"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Name","validations":[],"valueType":"StringQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:07Z","entityUuid":"235b36a8-3df7-44b7-9d0f-2ced3e4281a3","parentUuid":"b8543a67-2a6b-4f45-a0b0-d245227f9818","uuid":"8f0b5248-9d2b-4632-93ea-6abc40de5184"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"PID for the software, or URL where the software can be found","validations":[],"valueType":"StringQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2020-11-11T10:50:08Z","entityUuid":"f29e2dbd-8edc-4ac3-92ba-96a6d507789b","parentUuid":"b8543a67-2a6b-4f45-a0b