uid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:04:47Z","entityUuid":"eb711ea8-8ee7-40b1-a56d-1a374fe8b4c2","parentUuid":"7fc8d3c9-a2d5-4d47-9df4-56af48ca85e1","uuid":"99e8a5e7-1004-4e88-8915-0dff6ffce766"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:04:48Z","entityUuid":"4e0141ae-bec4-492e-98f4-b79a32c7e946","parentUuid":"042540a6-5b4a-483d-af23-f33b486d85f5","uuid":"ba4d6dcc-3551-4489-9fe5-443df767809c"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:04:49Z","entityUuid":"f5e129dc-d59d-4352-a5ed-25efe1d83811","parentUuid":"be872000-cb98-442f-999c-ca3ef58dcfe8","uuid":"fba7a8a3-5303-4aab-a628-1bffb7cde5ca"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.3.4","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.3","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.3.4"},{"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:02.002951Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ListQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":"Please list any references to other data sets, e.g. from your project or from earlier research. Note: A qualified reference is a cross-reference that explains its intent. For example, X is regulator of Y is a much more qualified reference than X is associated with Y, or X see also Y. The goal therefore is to create as many meaningful links as possible between (meta)data resources to enrich the contextual knowledge about the data","title":"Qualified references to other data sets"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:03Z","entityUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"e2fd499c-e3de-4265-9ad9-2e2b73501637"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"FAIR principle \"I3\"","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/i3-metadata-include-qualified-references-metadata/"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:04Z","entityUuid":"c57507b2-9581-465d-ba9a-7dcd8cfab8c0","parentUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","uuid":"2483c03a-9309-4bfb-95e7-3ad7f2da364d"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Please list any references to other data sets, e.g. from your project or from earlier research. \n\nNote: A qualified reference is a cross-reference that explains its intent. For example, X is regulator of Y is a much more qualified reference than X is associated with Y, or X see also Y. The goal therefore is to create as many meaningful links as possible between (meta)data resources to enrich the contextual knowledge about the data."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:05Z","entityUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"960f3330-8279-4e45-9681-a9a70aba752d"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Identifier of the data set that will be referred to","validations":[],"valueType":"StringQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:06Z","entityUuid":"abb6ac92-6508-4a24-b262-5d64db4ae731","parentUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","uuid":"3b029e33-ecd9-4ac7-9245-b18ac59f458b"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"The relationship between this dataset and the referred data set","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:07Z","entityUuid":"c70e49f9-09e4-456a-814b-bbaa8fde887c","parentUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","uuid":"4a5fa4b8-4f42-41f4-8c32-f98dbf212be2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":true,"value":"adc9133d-afcd-4616-9aea-db5f475898a2"},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Which qualified references to other data sets will be included"}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:08Z","entityUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"b6e8ab0e-f2be-4a17-90db-322dc6f9d978"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"color":"#3498DB","description":null,"eventType":"AddTagEvent","name":"Horizon Europe DMP"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:09Z","entityUuid":"87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","parentUuid":"6f6241d9-136c-4770-9d58-8a3f39607052","uuid":"979f6cd4-79f4-4f9a-b8e7-8f926eb43eb6"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"color":{"changed":true,"value":"#2ECC71"},"description":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditTagEvent","name":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:10Z","entityUuid":"87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","parentUuid":"6f6241d9-136c-4770-9d58-8a3f39607052","uuid":"fedf8a09-b40f-4bfc-80f6-57550cb39ffa"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"color":{"changed":false},"description":{"changed":true,"value":"Questions related to the Horizon Europe DMP"},"eventType":"EditTagEvent","name":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:11Z","entityUuid":"87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","parentUuid":"6f6241d9-136c-4770-9d58-8a3f39607052","uuid":"9080f0f1-47cf-4e9f-a883-e84327dfabdd"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:12Z","entityUuid":"7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd","parentUuid":"8d1b07a7-f177-41f5-9532-05536223a8d6","uuid":"82e8470c-731c-42f9-9371-da5c807a929a"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","19b0fe70-a884-4539-96b9-a0aaf8c9b884","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:13Z","entityUuid":"efc80cc8-8318-4f8c-acb7-dc1c60e491c1","parentUuid":"82fd0cce-2b41-423f-92ad-636d0872045c","uuid":"32fdd3f9-72f4-4cf6-b4bb-836432481057"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:14Z","entityUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","parentUuid":"2663b978-5125-4224-9930-0a50dbe895c9","uuid":"723e9cca-3e43-4d08-8eba-860613a3e0a7"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:15Z","entityUuid":"58401091-2d48-4231-983a-c972d11d9f6e","parentUuid":"fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010","uuid":"f33073e9-6335-40d3-a4a9-8e2d83518f3f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","19b0fe70-a884-4539-96b9-a0aaf8c9b884","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:16Z","entityUuid":"be872000-cb98-442f-999c-ca3ef58dcfe8","parentUuid":"2663b978-5125-4224-9930-0a50dbe895c9","uuid":"06559ee2-cdbd-46e4-83e0-d7dde89894b2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:17Z","entityUuid":"f5e129dc-d59d-4352-a5ed-25efe1d83811","parentUuid":"be872000-cb98-442f-999c-ca3ef58dcfe8","uuid":"42bbb539-dda3-470e-b5cb-934f85979fea"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:18Z","entityUuid":"eb711ea8-8ee7-40b1-a56d-1a374fe8b4c2","parentUuid":"7fc8d3c9-a2d5-4d47-9df4-56af48ca85e1","uuid":"f47c477e-eca2-43b0-bf85-6cd8a9f2fb89"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:19Z","entityUuid":"4e0141ae-bec4-492e-98f4-b79a32c7e946","parentUuid":"042540a6-5b4a-483d-af23-f33b486d85f5","uuid":"9fc3ddaf-b5c2-46ca-9df8-3e1a10b6f315"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:20Z","entityUuid":"d45ad247-19d4-4919-9a6c-094f696168b6","parentUuid":"81642493-5919-42c6-b9b7-af4cdbe1937b","uuid":"6262d728-17eb-4e41-a761-a549fc3636c2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T11:57:21Z","entityUuid":"bf02f456-0a60-4b50-ae86-5cd56d430b2e","parentUuid":"8a1937d8-39dc-4efd-a3f6-b62e789f225b","uuid":"5b0c564b-c875-45f0-9096-f38381e63e48"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.3.5","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.4","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.3.5"},{"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:02.158721Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"],"text":null,"title":"Will you be including keywords to optimise the possibility for discovery and potential reuse?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:03Z","entityUuid":"c37476ca-0f0f-47a9-87b2-505a67b83558","parentUuid":"aec37b0d-490d-4d75-8814-8ed78ea5b8dd","uuid":"f9ed7148-a931-4bdb-bf48-e8557f319d8d"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[{"measure":0,"metricUuid":"8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a","weight":1}]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:04Z","entityUuid":"ca706a0f-ef35-4ee6-ba48-c73a4c33dafe","parentUuid":"c37476ca-0f0f-47a9-87b2-505a67b83558","uuid":"8c9cd6eb-d123-42c2-91dc-4b7ddca87ed8"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:05Z","entityUuid":"c37476ca-0f0f-47a9-87b2-505a67b83558","parentUuid":"aec37b0d-490d-4d75-8814-8ed78ea5b8dd","uuid":"42134fba-bd9c-481f-8e5c-5b1cef13aa83"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[{"measure":1,"metricUuid":"8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a","weight":1}]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:06Z","entityUuid":"b6cb254e-f243-4a43-af2d-72864d51969e","parentUuid":"c37476ca-0f0f-47a9-87b2-505a67b83558","uuid":"a96ec18f-d55d-4c73-bc45-2ac325cf98a2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Will you be including keywords or relevant ontology references to optimise the possibility for discovery and potential reuse?"}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:07Z","entityUuid":"c37476ca-0f0f-47a9-87b2-505a67b83558","parentUuid":"aec37b0d-490d-4d75-8814-8ed78ea5b8dd","uuid":"7472df7f-b792-4e37-a66d-7be31a69879d"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"],"text":"Horizon Europe demands that metadata is completely open, e.g. provided under a CC0 license, and that any deviation from this is clarified.","title":"Will metadata be available openly?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:08Z","entityUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","parentUuid":"6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd","uuid":"b74bfb49-5fcd-4cb8-9914-7e7a80995567"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:09Z","entityUuid":"1dc216a6-77df-4f75-8bab-8e4f082fdab2","parentUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","uuid":"2584189b-5618-4cdd-8c1c-8b20b4f516db"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:10Z","entityUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","parentUuid":"6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd","uuid":"140ba2ea-7429-4705-83bd-b2eca3e3776a"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[{"measure":1,"metricUuid":"8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a","weight":1}]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:11Z","entityUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","parentUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","uuid":"077bf98a-c2c1-4f48-b513-197f86ee6283"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":true,"value":[{"measure":0,"metricUuid":"8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a","weight":1}]}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:12Z","entityUuid":"1dc216a6-77df-4f75-8bab-8e4f082fdab2","parentUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","uuid":"3d93f79e-79e8-4b9c-ae1b-803d0b136d2e"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:13Z","entityUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","parentUuid":"6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd","uuid":"f776d038-b951-4001-9174-f862a27991a2"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":true,"value":[{"measure":0,"metricUuid":"0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7","weight":1}]}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:14Z","entityUuid":"1dc216a6-77df-4f75-8bab-8e4f082fdab2","parentUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","uuid":"3887e150-a47d-4962-bbc0-ccafc59385e4"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":true,"value":[{"measure":1,"metricUuid":"0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7","weight":1}]}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:15Z","entityUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","parentUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","uuid":"91ea527d-be77-42c3-937d-3a868ae31885"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"],"text":null,"title":"Please explain why the metadata will not be openly available","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:16Z","entityUuid":"6b5a6334-fbb3-4c88-995a-6d899e30da1e","parentUuid":"1dc216a6-77df-4f75-8bab-8e4f082fdab2","uuid":"7577735c-8dfd-4985-bb29-59884b85993f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:17Z","entityUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","parentUuid":"6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd","uuid":"09f44432-02ca-4011-886a-d0155e8d4adc"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e","tagUuids":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"],"text":null,"title":"Will metadata contain instructions how to get access to the data?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:18Z","entityUuid":"26b2afa6-99e8-4337-b380-5642bc807ad8","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"7d546532-0faa-4163-bb93-8e581abe95a8"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:19Z","entityUuid":"12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a","parentUuid":"6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd","uuid":"a77f1fb3-18e3-44af-bede-e7112f42632a"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":"Repositories often allow search engines and catalogues to index the metadata in an automated way. Will this be the case for your data?","title":"Will the metadata be available in a form that can be harvested and indexed?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:20Z","entityUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"fe88db16-6140-4278-b5b4-a507b051d622"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[{"measure":0,"metricUuid":"0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7","weight":1}]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:21Z","entityUuid":"e3f7a89a-2d34-4b44-81bf-773b1d8cd2e3","parentUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","uuid":"8b122faf-56a9-46f1-9e40-a204c1db386f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:22Z","entityUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"9554b1c0-9c52-4fc7-a477-27a94aa72546"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes, by the repository / repositories","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:23Z","entityUuid":"6833a1fa-62fe-46b1-bb81-a3e42ff9626d","parentUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","uuid":"0d12662c-c919-4c20-94d9-7f97c068343b"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":true,"value":"1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e"},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:24Z","entityUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"6a6e495b-6874-4653-89d8-2a5acf9ad13b"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes, we will take care of that","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:25Z","entityUuid":"90bd5ae9-087f-429d-8e2a-d322078f1d20","parentUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","uuid":"9de62d65-d7d7-4b71-a2bf-893ee17f199d"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:26Z","entityUuid":"26b2afa6-99e8-4337-b380-5642bc807ad8","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"80bff201-7d2c-4d99-b0b4-9321f615b820"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:27Z","entityUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"bf3cbf75-2d06-456f-b2e2-d76d03448eb7"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":true,"value":[{"measure":1,"metricUuid":"0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7","weight":1}]}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:28Z","entityUuid":"6833a1fa-62fe-46b1-bb81-a3e42ff9626d","parentUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","uuid":"9e9fa1f1-5cae-4c05-96e9-0780612c074e"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":true,"value":[{"measure":1,"metricUuid":"0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7","weight":1}]}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:29Z","entityUuid":"90bd5ae9-087f-429d-8e2a-d322078f1d20","parentUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","uuid":"7908a48e-a165-4f3c-a615-2b0cf4a3424d"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-10T14:44:30Z","entityUuid":"1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57","parentUuid":"cb148cc8-f15f-494f-a197-f01e3111ec60","uuid":"9f452671-36f1-490e-b65c-353c91e4e81d"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.3.6","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.5","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.3.6\r\n* Questions about metadata for Horizon Europe added [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 4-6]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.3.6"},{"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:52.898625Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Did you get an ethical committee to make an ethical review on your project?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:53Z","entityUuid":"3782d32b-91b5-432f-8f93-92bb22868a22","parentUuid":"421e2d3e-c95c-4244-9465-de8f1cb8aeba","uuid":"41fb29c3-f4e6-4f35-a369-5821ab85d65d"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:54Z","entityUuid":"6480ac87-faaa-4b47-9a66-f338e95ace5a","parentUuid":"3782d32b-91b5-432f-8f93-92bb22868a22","uuid":"90a8fa73-dafe-4bd0-9854-1ad75dfe4d81"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:55Z","entityUuid":"04644b31-678c-45d5-807d-93d0d79f2221","parentUuid":"3782d32b-91b5-432f-8f93-92bb22868a22","uuid":"0974790f-7eab-4e3f-827b-cfd773f41ef8"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":"It is important for re-users to know what consent items you asked exactly from participants.","title":"Will the consent form be available for re-users?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:56Z","entityUuid":"d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42","parentUuid":"73cd2dda-41ba-456b-9a4e-aa34c78f2fcf","uuid":"a14c3afe-a4c3-4ea9-a397-3f9d0c740d6a"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:57Z","entityUuid":"e4b4093e-9abd-40ce-bd9a-8720b2966017","parentUuid":"d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42","uuid":"910e0dde-58bb-4376-99bd-57e097b6d839"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:58Z","entityUuid":"dce67815-b47b-4e92-a70e-b32735cf9e5b","parentUuid":"d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42","uuid":"87edc2b0-dc15-45d8-bc9c-5f850a15a2bb"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"It is important for re-users to know what consent items you asked exactly from participants.\n\nNote that the answers from participants is personal data that requires protection!"},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:54:59Z","entityUuid":"d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42","parentUuid":"73cd2dda-41ba-456b-9a4e-aa34c78f2fcf","uuid":"c52620c4-28a8-4d10-9c12-aa8de144c334"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Human Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/human_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:00Z","entityUuid":"612660d5-dedc-4c4d-9176-06a887b47f14","parentUuid":"49c009cb-a38c-4836-9780-8a8b3dd1cbac","uuid":"64147d03-32d7-4712-b381-6f50759154c7"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Human Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/human_data.html#processing-and-analysing-human-research-data"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:01Z","entityUuid":"2a6ffbc9-6a07-4d5a-8df6-e7c44ce2356c","parentUuid":"d5990471-0618-42cd-92cb-bbbfd4f61532","uuid":"fe84ca1b-5fc8-487b-9a0b-afdccce6da8b"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sensitive Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/sensitive_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:02Z","entityUuid":"86f7c739-cfdf-4b3a-a032-3bda9bbf6404","parentUuid":"59748a7b-f729-404d-babe-3147e2c6b247","uuid":"501d0fea-9787-4fc9-985a-4ab3f4ee1d9f"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Note that it is very hard to make data anonymous, and GDPR requires that you regularly verify that it is still anonymous."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:03Z","entityUuid":"ca0df149-cb95-404a-a925-0a1fc5052d1d","parentUuid":"d5990471-0618-42cd-92cb-bbbfd4f61532","uuid":"c3dc05a3-4848-4305-9486-0dc52f673986"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Please note that GDPR law in Europe specifies that data is only anonymous as long as nobody in the world has enough information to re-identify the subject.\n\nFurthermore, GDPR requires that you regularly verify that it is still anonymous."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:04Z","entityUuid":"44348fa8-fd12-49ea-ad7f-48ff88215829","parentUuid":"d5990471-0618-42cd-92cb-bbbfd4f61532","uuid":"afc444b1-29a0-4f33-8829-9f26c977f173"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Who is the independent party that keeps the pseudonymization?","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:05Z","entityUuid":"5d51a103-ec07-4c20-b269-f2f59f26d2cd","parentUuid":"1653a04e-20e2-4929-9fd5-8c35402ac359","uuid":"947cf4c9-d458-41f2-bc50-77dbe9a837b8"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"Who is the independent party that keeps the pseudonymization keys?"},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:06Z","entityUuid":"5d51a103-ec07-4c20-b269-f2f59f26d2cd","parentUuid":"1653a04e-20e2-4929-9fd5-8c35402ac359","uuid":"6334c713-3e10-4bad-9016-0534ba49aac7"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sensitive Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/sensitive_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:07Z","entityUuid":"00af9ed1-2627-45d7-89e8-63876fd92a2f","parentUuid":"6b3d62a5-1d4d-49e1-aaf1-0a8b398a7ac3","uuid":"745f8ccc-a4cd-40be-84c3-3b386c937a94"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sensitive Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/sensitive_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:08Z","entityUuid":"68a9e378-e7ef-48bd-9e65-62937f7804d0","parentUuid":"a1d76760-053c-4706-80a2-cfb6c6a061f3","uuid":"480ad988-5de8-46e4-8a29-a068ad6a8e55"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sensitive Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/sensitive_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:09Z","entityUuid":"4302bc15-31f1-42c0-b921-183847404605","parentUuid":"cc95b399-7d8d-4232-bccf-686f78c91bff","uuid":"1a41271f-22f4-41b6-97af-fe6a1869798e"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddChoiceEvent","label":"Data Protection Officer"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:10Z","entityUuid":"bc82b138-9816-46dd-8ff8-cea2826a3ad4","parentUuid":"829dcda6-db8a-40ac-819a-92b9b52490f5","uuid":"d2034899-662b-4647-8915-f02ec67575eb"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"choiceUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["2c6ee59d-4dc9-4dcb-ac13-d969c317a117","fc789e2d-01ee-432d-82f9-1b659f58eaf8","618cb529-0c24-4762-a739-7983004d1b2b","627ab8dc-8026-498d-ba7a-3df122e29ede","bc82b138-9816-46dd-8ff8-cea2826a3ad4","3022098b-0e2c-4fad-9f28-cf2e1325521d","27dccf06-3b67-4c75-8888-6549e4da2d31","100daf28-b55e-4b04-8295-f2aa83d0c734","2085d67e-e144-4ec2-a788-1b26ac1cd7ab","2d433965-55e3-4540-aae4-f85639d4e4fc","cd2d1e0d-c5ad-4d0e-afa2-5ed143323cb7","3d166766-6511-407b-a3e9-9565628fe05a","c81c63b6-bec0-4e12-b9cd-247fa4338c1f","704ebc65-6932-4679-bbe5-f25c19843f0f","374b887f-dfd8-4763-b360-b2a8aa12051c","6dfde2b6-4234-47a0-b7da-ccb7412f8490","ce5476ed-5cc3-42ff-ac9d-d567f28cc2a6","e957ecd5-baa2-4a3c-aaf1-735d416e5e11"]},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"MultiChoiceQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:11Z","entityUuid":"829dcda6-db8a-40ac-819a-92b9b52490f5","parentUuid":"73d686bd-7939-412e-8631-502ee6d9ea7b","uuid":"faec0748-9c7c-4f37-ad3e-7c2ac94bf560"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":"You need a DPIA whenever you deal with any personal data under the European GDPR, almost for any biomedical research.","title":"Do you need a Data Protection Impact Assessment?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:12Z","entityUuid":"8915bd25-db22-4ed6-bcc8-b1bbdc52989e","parentUuid":"421e2d3e-c95c-4244-9465-de8f1cb8aeba","uuid":"810ab96d-7e78-458c-a1ec-206dad8ec52a"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"No","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:13Z","entityUuid":"d0741ff3-370b-44e7-860d-00b1f01e6254","parentUuid":"8915bd25-db22-4ed6-bcc8-b1bbdc52989e","uuid":"16b1e9c1-a6e3-4d77-a0b0-f677993e4330"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Yes","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:14Z","entityUuid":"c3914e43-cca1-4180-8960-228b7022bae6","parentUuid":"8915bd25-db22-4ed6-bcc8-b1bbdc52989e","uuid":"e8ed20eb-4dd9-4949-a146-982084c61afb"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Data Protection","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/data_protection.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:15Z","entityUuid":"ba4eb06a-2d61-4755-bb51-8232b349d0a1","parentUuid":"8915bd25-db22-4ed6-bcc8-b1bbdc52989e","uuid":"7d650cf2-2e2d-4dce-8977-8ccaa228ef90"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditReferenceEvent","label":{"changed":true,"value":"RDMkit about Sensitive Data"},"referenceType":"URLReference","url":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:16Z","entityUuid":"df93fa41-88cb-451a-aa05-95a18cf02e73","parentUuid":"49c009cb-a38c-4836-9780-8a8b3dd1cbac","uuid":"63262f32-e042-4fc0-bf3c-edef31e2d489"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Data Protection","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/data_protection.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:17Z","entityUuid":"42a7b822-5644-48f5-aa9a-9a9e3119a028","parentUuid":"49c009cb-a38c-4836-9780-8a8b3dd1cbac","uuid":"e50da616-3fc7-42ac-8061-b6c560c39f22"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sharing Human Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/human_data.html#sharing-and-reusing-of-human-research-data"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:18Z","entityUuid":"ff3b29fc-fa24-4799-aa2c-29fabc5fc584","parentUuid":"55f03a4a-034b-422a-adf6-757416b7650a","uuid":"57d4f495-25a8-4a12-bad7-df8aacdc82f6"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"RDMkit on Sensitive Data","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/sensitive_data.html"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:19Z","entityUuid":"f22531ad-862e-48fa-a521-18e6998b1f7d","parentUuid":"019db0b3-9067-4134-8bfd-76db3cfc572a","uuid":"cb5d1d29-df70-456b-8fe3-f365c22806a3"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"Where do you keep any applicable restrictions on the usage of the data?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:20Z","entityUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","parentUuid":"421e2d3e-c95c-4244-9465-de8f1cb8aeba","uuid":"db2125b6-f6ba-48ea-8ad5-9fb54b817f13"},{"content":{"eventType":"MoveQuestionEvent","targetUuid":"6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:21Z","entityUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","parentUuid":"421e2d3e-c95c-4244-9465-de8f1cb8aeba","uuid":"7d4a9a26-8918-4704-a25e-54139be206cc"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":false},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["1440afd6-d516-44f6-9c02-6abb13900b66","6226d7f2-565f-4991-94b3-c00be6aca20e","ed872b74-6bf7-4cba-8f36-4da4509e4a4f","15573266-7ddf-4c6b-962e-45691d34cf61","ae28a862-5020-44c2-8c78-3abc185b190f","de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","948b5fd8-c1bd-457d-8f81-ea2fd093f541","106df534-f590-416b-8e4a-846edbdc4325","91a7c75c-6f0e-4bae-b3f3-1890feaae9b2"]},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:22Z","entityUuid":"6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb","parentUuid":"8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3","uuid":"0cf7142d-024e-4ba2-93e8-64e7cc25fcf0"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"In a specialised registry or catalogue","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:23Z","entityUuid":"5458a4cb-b4b1-400f-bc7e-df45bbeb42af","parentUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","uuid":"a811ee2b-9ca0-4d71-864a-1d34413ab279"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Closely attached to the data in the data management system","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:24Z","entityUuid":"ff6ea5fb-c987-4391-bca7-c3c3e7a95964","parentUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","uuid":"f45fb7d7-6a50-448f-993d-32ee9c846505"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"Stored in the same folder as the data","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:25Z","entityUuid":"eefe3d60-b037-488a-826c-871490357ffc","parentUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","uuid":"49ad4615-b0f3-484a-9d97-79a6af408419"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"In another way","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:26Z","entityUuid":"0cdaa526-aa38-47d6-aa28-e8eaa8a3b127","parentUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","uuid":"6bd26c64-a8fd-4517-94a0-126e0eb408e0"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"ValueQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":"How will you store any applicable restrictions?","validations":[],"valueType":"TextQuestionValueType"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:27Z","entityUuid":"f9572d3c-c91f-4945-a56b-ccfb32750fe9","parentUuid":"0cdaa526-aa38-47d6-aa28-e8eaa8a3b127","uuid":"02244801-9903-4432-a9e2-fc5b6f24c66d"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddReferenceEvent","label":"Data Use Ontology","referenceType":"URLReference","url":"https://github.com/EBISPOT/DUO#readme"},"createdAt":"2022-01-11T13:55:28Z","entityUuid":"35bcd464-9a68-49f3-8365-677fca660b17","parentUuid":"de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395","uuid":"8f97fc42-c181-41fd-a80b-ab1e6c5b170d"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.3.7","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.6","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.3.7\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Human Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.6\r\n* Questions about metadata for Horizon Europe added [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 4-6]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.3.7"},{"createdAt":"2022-01-14T16:07:23.062537Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"],"text":null,"title":"Who will be paying for the long term storage?"},"createdAt":"2022-01-14T16:07:24Z","entityUuid":"6467fff1-33ae-47f6-829c-9e3817298d1f","parentUuid":"562a4823-3e58-44da-ba65-db522c4bbbd9","uuid":"42e97caa-6572-4604-8f39-00d53483b4d9"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"It will be paid from the grant","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-01-14T16:07:25Z","entityUuid":"3aabde57-dabd-456f-b351-1b81a74bb2d5","parentUuid":"6467fff1-33ae-47f6-829c-9e3817298d1f","uuid":"fc44f4df-9b95-448b-87ae-3e35cc2baaee"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"v