alse},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:44Z","entityUuid":"f9d84278-b61d-4314-94e9-12644bfa1d00","parentUuid":"d5b27482-b598-4b8c-b534-417d4ad27394","uuid":"abf78e12-1e92-42f8-b592-aa20e877a875"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:45Z","entityUuid":"530124a4-c7e9-4821-b26d-32a8ecd0d978","parentUuid":"4a3e9d91-240b-4eae-bc90-02c12a2a4744","uuid":"c3416e21-2ebd-4152-bfbe-d71cff3768a2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:46Z","entityUuid":"d45ad247-19d4-4919-9a6c-094f696168b6","parentUuid":"81642493-5919-42c6-b9b7-af4cdbe1937b","uuid":"268f42c8-f92a-4fcd-9645-e31766bbc428"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:47Z","entityUuid":"ed3d43ad-d2b5-4194-8b05-08c95da0a7f2","parentUuid":"e81599af-4519-4987-b74e-9545428ed0e3","uuid":"56623689-c040-4a1f-a4e2-54c3123c770f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:48Z","entityUuid":"e24167a2-14ec-445d-b205-fb6c7e24a7d1","parentUuid":"f1e2f788-0957-4111-b342-ab9797641e4d","uuid":"ea10741b-675e-4c65-87a8-a7a3399111ec"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ValueQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["3c7bdc90-8ed3-4b34-90ec-7945d14cc443","19b0fe70-a884-4539-96b9-a0aaf8c9b884","fd4637a2-a117-460a-a7fa-c03760c42629","87bb2042-8e3c-4733-ba1e-84509d7b1cf4"]},"text":{"changed":false},"title":{"changed":false},"validations":{"changed":false},"valueType":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-02-05T12:03:49Z","entityUuid":"22583d74-3c98-4e0a-b363-26d767c88212","parentUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","uuid":"2fc52137-1c99-4daa-974d-37d4ad74d514"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.3.14","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.13","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.3.14\r\n\r\n* Tags for Horizon Europe template generated\r\n\r\n### 2.3.13\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Reuse workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.12\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Analytics workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.11\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes made in the Plant Sciences workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.10\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Preserving Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.9\r\n\r\n* Fix missing Yes/No answers and use Text-Value for description of policies\r\n\r\n### 2.3.8\r\n\r\n* Questions for Horizon Europe added on budget for data management, other policies that are observed, persistent identifier allocation and archive preservation policies [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 7-9, 11]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.7\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Human Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.6\r\n\r\n* Questions about metadata for Horizon Europe added [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 4-6]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.3.14"},{"createdAt":"2022-03-15T12:51:44.952848Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originating from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.4.0","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.3.14","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.4.0\r\n\r\n* KM verified and tested with the **Horizon Europe DMP template**\r\n\r\n### 2.3.14\r\n\r\n* Tags for Horizon Europe template generated\r\n\r\n### 2.3.13\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Reuse workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.12\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Analytics workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.11\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes made in the Plant Sciences workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.10\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Preserving Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.9\r\n\r\n* Fix missing Yes/No answers and use Text-Value for description of policies\r\n\r\n### 2.3.8\r\n\r\n* Questions for Horizon Europe added on budget for data management, other policies that are observed, persistent identifier allocation and archive preservation policies [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 7-9, 11]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.7\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Human Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.6\r\n\r\n* Questions about metadata for Horizon Europe added [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 4-6]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.4.0"},{"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:46:39.041058Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originating from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"If the intermediate results are in your main work space, a restore in case of a problem could take much more time. It may be faster to recover it by re-running computations."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:33:18Z","entityUuid":"deb647ec-a001-4370-87b8-a5b1e2479f87","parentUuid":"9a0cfd22-adce-46e6-b7ec-8ed581ac95be","uuid":"2b16d4aa-1e3b-4b7d-81df-84fea800c99f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Are there any data files e.g. on laptops of project members? Also: supercomputing centers and other high performance computer centers often write in their terms of use that you need to take care of your own backups."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:33:33Z","entityUuid":"98d9789b-32fc-4e2f-876a-47760ad7c7ec","parentUuid":"0d64d3c6-4312-47a9-92ad-0bc9440d6e45","uuid":"8bd9f6c5-b8a9-449e-8487-28e9cb5b96d2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Some \"file\" storage systems do not have a tree structure like we know in a file system, but rather have direct pointers to any file in the system. Such systems are called \"object store\". Examples are Amazon S3 and CEPH."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:33:49Z","entityUuid":"dc39957e-688a-4f71-a6a8-57f52509e7cf","parentUuid":"f7f2ff16-eee0-42a7-a89a-bd7291cef5fc","uuid":"f2df3661-a8a2-43b0-a1cf-74d142c7d1ac"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Your workflow may be available in components from different sources. Specify the different parts that you recognize and that you will each acquire in a different way."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:34:06Z","entityUuid":"9a1c0153-3eae-40d5-8e91-66e108ef1fe8","parentUuid":"bb00eb32-e1c2-4288-a874-02264f757cb3","uuid":"6484da16-519e-49d7-8da9-5a9df41201ed"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Project members may need to know about passwords (not sharing accounts, using different passwords for each service, and two factor authentication), about security for data they carry (encryption, backups), data stored in their own labs and in personal cloud accounts, and about the use of open WiFi and HTTPS."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:34:23Z","entityUuid":"dc327e53-cf4f-44e7-8e66-40ddf1b4ae0a","parentUuid":"b2f76c0a-847a-403c-9ed6-09cad10e625e","uuid":"791c524a-6e78-425c-a27e-127797f57fb9"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"It is advisable to make the result of your efforts available in a standard repository. If you answer 'yes' here, do not forget to mention the dataset under the chapter 'giving access to data'."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:34:35Z","entityUuid":"530124a4-c7e9-4821-b26d-32a8ecd0d978","parentUuid":"4a3e9d91-240b-4eae-bc90-02c12a2a4744","uuid":"8881902f-b0dc-4cdb-be6a-c853aef9a6d1"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"By publishing either exactly what you did or (better) make sure that the harmonized data is available for reuse, you may save others the effort."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:34:53Z","entityUuid":"1d1ac8bb-66c8-4b9e-bfc9-4c26f3598062","parentUuid":"a62a452b-dfed-478c-ad94-0e433277da94","uuid":"7836ed24-268b-408c-bcab-491e456dd8cb"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Consider storing only the workflow parameters if the data itself could be reproduced quickly."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:35:03Z","entityUuid":"89f78871-68bd-4190-9ee7-57ec3b4c2356","parentUuid":"aca843cd-e38e-4174-8ce1-477c2b405fdf","uuid":"fb37a0c3-3970-45ba-96d1-49e1fe703903"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Think about services like Dropbox, but also about Google Drive, Apple iCloud accounts, or Microsoft Office 365."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:35:27Z","entityUuid":"84ec46bd-e714-4d98-8525-cdd0d58777ef","parentUuid":"b2f76c0a-847a-403c-9ed6-09cad10e625e","uuid":"ab5f215a-0aa2-4d16-845b-a35bd6591564"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Make sure your users are aware of the risks of cloud storage (not so much that the cloud is unreliable, but there is no protection against \"accidentally\" sharing a cloud folder with people outside the project)."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:35:54Z","entityUuid":"b5e75eac-3db1-4736-8b22-7f8ed99218ab","parentUuid":"84ec46bd-e714-4d98-8525-cdd0d58777ef","uuid":"5ae70358-b2e4-4533-887c-db4131b9612a"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Making use of the same pseudonymization for different studies makes it possible to integrate information later. Obviously it also raises the risk of re-identification."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:36:17Z","entityUuid":"5db6bd58-5d1d-4d02-9497-972cbef64c16","parentUuid":"49f268a6-9566-4aa4-bec3-44fec2e64548","uuid":"6cf0f349-de53-4d57-890d-36f24d3bae8e"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Different anonymization techniques exist. Disadvantage of anonymization is that data integration becomes virtually impossible, but it may be the only way to open up your data for other research."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:37:04Z","entityUuid":"15ee1921-1fea-4f22-b462-b3cf7cdd4646","parentUuid":"8a56768a-5c5a-44c0-b21c-46a231fbf6be","uuid":"27b100f2-b26a-439a-8618-29e4b49e467f"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Aggregated data, where typically at least 15 individuals are in any data point, are considered sufficiently anonymous. This is an alternative way of making data openly available for future research."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:37:14Z","entityUuid":"69be6695-152b-48ba-a1fd-6662476e39b7","parentUuid":"8a56768a-5c5a-44c0-b21c-46a231fbf6be","uuid":"79d99ee1-0916-43db-a6a9-3ad7834c77a5"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Linked data is very suitable to integrate data, especially if the data sources are already represented as linked data."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:38:06Z","entityUuid":"ff85db18-565c-4177-a397-9a8cf4c7b374","parentUuid":"238ace4b-22bb-4a9d-a312-e30d82d4382d","uuid":"8835a672-0865-444f-b730-5810c9e47e64"},{"content":{"advice":{"changed":true,"value":"Choose the ontologies before you start."},"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditAnswerEvent","followUpUuids":{"changed":false},"label":{"changed":false},"metricMeasures":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:40:04Z","entityUuid":"3e5ef321-76f3-4c65-a49f-4e03f6a23def","parentUuid":"f67e1539-5c7d-4df7-8259-e4f2edfa2685","uuid":"a6376c4f-748e-4ed3-9537-bab16c2d31fe"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"If there are reasonable limitations to the values in a column, or even a limited set of allowed values, it is very good for data validation and reusability if these limitations are explicit, and e.g. software used for data entry and editing will not allow anything else."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:41:24Z","entityUuid":"c47d330a-2eb4-472e-be48-d06b3ec9b8e8","parentUuid":"53d43c6a-d12e-4bfd-b70d-233bf62c7f5b","uuid":"a360da13-ba1a-4eb5-a9e3-1b7b5b5848b2"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"For the re-usability of your data by yourself or others at a later stage, a lot of information about the data – for example how it was collected and how it can be used – should be stored with the data. Such *data about the data* is called **metadata**, and this set of questions are about this metadata."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:41:57Z","entityUuid":"8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3","parentUuid":"b1df3c74-0b1f-4574-81c4-4cc2d780c1af","uuid":"54517cf8-5230-491b-8591-ceaefd97725c"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Add each of the research project(s) that you are (or will be) working on and for which the data and work are described in this DMP. Give each project a small identifying name for yourself."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:42:48Z","entityUuid":"c3dabaaf-c946-4a0d-889c-ede966f97667","parentUuid":"1e85da40-bbfc-4180-903e-6c569ed2da38","uuid":"b7aaf6a7-c6ed-4e2b-b2f3-7831c189eb81"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"answerUuids":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"OptionsQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":false},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"It is very likely that data will be moved and copied. At some point people may lose track of the origins. It can be helpful to have the licenses (of course *as open as possible*) stored in close association with the data."},"title":{"changed":false}},"createdAt":"2022-04-09T10:43:25Z","entityUuid":"0551adc9-7faa-4ddc-a07b-08fbde2a247b","parentUuid":"6110d79f-1cf0-4a89-8a6d-84a472388fd8","uuid":"86d7f27b-ff8e-4ee4-ab6d-9c63e2d7433a"}],"forkOfPackageId":null,"id":"dsw:root:2.4.1","kmId":"root","language":"en","license":"Apache-2.0","mergeCheckpointPackageId":null,"metamodelVersion":20,"name":"Common DSW Knowledge Model","nonEditable":false,"organizationId":"dsw","phase":"DeprecatedKnowledgeModelPackagePhase","previousPackageId":"dsw:root:2.4.0","readme":"# Common DSW Knowledge Model\r\n\r\nCommon DSW Knowledge Model deals with questions that a researcher should answer in order to create a Data Stewardship Plan, as well as other related questionnaire data. It originated from mindmap made by Rob Hooft.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\n### 2.4.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed several minor typos (missing end of sentence, misspelling, typography etc.)\r\n\r\n### 2.4.0\r\n\r\n* KM verified and tested with the **Horizon Europe DMP template**\r\n\r\n### 2.3.14\r\n\r\n* Tags for Horizon Europe template generated\r\n\r\n### 2.3.13\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Reuse workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.12\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes related to the Data Analytics workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.11\r\n\r\n* Incorporating changes made in the Plant Sciences workshop with RDMkit\r\n\r\n### 2.3.10\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Preserving Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.9\r\n\r\n* Fix missing Yes/No answers and use Text-Value for description of policies\r\n\r\n### 2.3.8\r\n\r\n* Questions for Horizon Europe added on budget for data management, other policies that are observed, persistent identifier allocation and archive preservation policies [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 7-9, 11]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.7\r\n\r\n* Added references and questions from an RDMkit/DS Wizard working session on Human Data\r\n\r\n### 2.3.6\r\n\r\n* Questions about metadata for Horizon Europe added [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issues 4-6]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.5\r\n\r\n* Added Tag for Horizon Europe\r\n* Moved the new questions from 2.3.4 from \"Science Europe\" to \"Horizon Europe\"\r\n* Added new question about qualified references from published data sets [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 3]\r\n\r\n### 2.3.4\r\n\r\n* Change lists of reused (non-)reference datasets that are reused into lists of considered datasets, and add a question for each detailing whether they are actually reused and what for / why not. This is to be included in the Science Europe template [Marek/Jana Horizon Europe issue 1 and 2].\r\n\r\n### 2.3.3\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a collaborative workshop with RDMkit participants on data processing.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit (and some to other external resources) in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Added question on data versioning for filesystems\r\n\r\n### 2.3.2\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data collecting.\r\n   * Added links to RDMkit in several places\r\n   * Clarified some questions\r\n   * Moved questions on quality together\r\n   * Moved some questions out of the metadata subsection\r\n\r\n### 2.3.1\r\n\r\n* Incorporation of changes from a workshop with the authors of the RDMkit page on data sharing.\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"accessible\"\r\n    * Attempt to clarify difference between \"open\" and \"embargoed\"\r\n    * Added links to RDMkit Data Sharing page in a few places\r\n    * Added a few relevant questions\r\n\r\n### 2.3.0\r\n\r\nActivity during [BioHackathon Europe](biohackathon-europe.org) 2020 ([#BioHackEU20](twitter.com/search?q=%23BioHackEU20))\r\n\r\n* Added and tagged questions for Horizon 2020 template\r\n* Moved questions about collecting metadata to one consistent place\r\n* Added guidance on semantics in file names and question about using PIDs for identifying files\r\n* Generic small cleanups and typo fixes\r\n* Closing many issues of feedback received on the knowledge model (from [DSWGlobal/dsw](https://github.com/DSWGlobal/dsw))\r\n* Various question updates new options, clarifications, integrations\r\n* Added highly configurable [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org) SPARQL-based integration\r\n* Added [Research Organization Registry](https://ror.org) integration for contributor's affiliation\r\n\r\n### 2.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adjusted for compatibility with [RDA DMP Common Standard for machine-actionable DMPs (1.0)](https://github.com/RDA-DMP-Common/RDA-DMP-Common-Standard)\r\n  * Updated *Project* and *Funding* questions in *Administrative Details* chapter\r\n  * Reorganised *Dataset*, *Distribution*, *License* questions in *Data Publishing* chapter\r\n* Added *maDMP* tag to questions used in the RDA maDMP template\r\n\r\n### 2.1.0\r\n\r\n* Added *Science Europe DMP* tag to questions used in the Science Europe template\r\n\r\n### 2.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fixed missing and duplicated questions\r\n\r\n### 2.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fixed duplicated question in *Creating and collecting data* chapter (5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030)\r\n\r\n### 2.0.0\r\n\r\n* Added detailed questions for Science Europe DMPs\r\n* Fixed several typos and other minor problems\r\n* Added administrative chapter\r\n* Moving questions and refactoring according to [ds-km#24](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/pull/24)\r\n\r\n### 1.4.0\r\n\r\n* Adding integration for [FAIRsharing.org](https://fairsharing.org)\r\n* Adding 5 integration questions according to [ds-km@da5a8fc](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/da5a8fc95d0a67f9369ce0b7727615115fc3656d)\r\n\r\nThe FAIRsharing integration requires configuration to contain `apiUrl` and `apiKey` for integration with id `fairsharing`.\r\n\r\n### 1.3.0\r\n\r\n* Refactoring list questions because of **deprecated item title** fields, i.e., a new question for item title created for each list question\r\n\r\nWhen using this version and higher, the DS Wizard configuration should have `itemTitleEnabled` set to `false`.\r\n\r\n### 1.2.0\r\n\r\n* Adding file naming SOP description question (9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f) to chapter 2 according to [ds-km@d879be0](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/d879be0fa9d0808868396c649d03c4d783ac6742)\r\n\r\n### 1.1.0\r\n\r\n* Adding phases to questions (first draft) according to [ds-km@a6713d1](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/a6713d1a4b9758bea63b3f7c56af5bd4f500d949) and [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\nPrior to this version, all questions were assigned with phase 2 - *Before submitting the DMP*.\r\n\r\n### 1.0.3\r\n\r\n* Fix: Removing extra question mark for a question (8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7) in chapter 5 according to: [ds-km@1123211](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/1123211bb5af43df8ef435039a2923f48e3e981c)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.2\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding some explanation to the list item questions (f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc and b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa) in chapter 3 according to: [ds-km@96e28f4](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/96e28f478d5dc6b59d384b5127f012dc2fe5f287)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.1\r\n\r\n* Fix: Adding forgotten question mark to end of question (39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923) in chapter 1 according to: [ds-km@644a373](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/644a373685dc4ac15b76e86667a90151ca9c70ca)\r\n\r\n### 1.0.0\r\n\r\n* Initial version transformed from the previous DS-KM GitHub repository up to [ds-km@8442837](https://github.com/ds-wizard/ds-km/commit/8442837dbe3ff899b09e7d8d3fc1107e935a876f)","version":"2.4.1"},{"createdAt":"2022-06-15T15:00:55.387477Z","description":"DSW Knowledge Model originating from mindmap made by Rob Hooft","events":[{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":""},"createdAt":"2022-04-12T09:33:10Z","entityUuid":"726e4a24-6d81-440b-8a70-5d36fa65c3a9","parentUuid":"82fd0cce-2b41-423f-92ad-636d0872045c","uuid":"e2b90e46-e95c-4111-9a63-645360ce8f27"},{"content":{"advice":null,"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddAnswerEvent","label":"","metricMeasures":[]},"createdAt":"2022-04-12T09:34:05Z","entityUuid":"5e632b7b-9b50-4a03-bc25-39a2b6af79f6","parentUuid":"726e4a24-6d81-440b-8a70-5d36fa65c3a9","uuid":"8d2368f0-6336-4394-bdef-99f0de306799"},{"content":{"advice":