ontent":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":""},"createdAt":"2022-02-28T14:44:08Z","entityUuid":"de72effc-807a-4081-b842-1e77ecc9c43f","parentUuid":"7dd7320e-41dd-43b9-b6aa-7622eaa34679","uuid":"fb1e177e-c948-4d24-bb35-c7fa071bffbc"},{"content":{"annotations":{"changed":false},"eventType":"EditQuestionEvent","expertUuids":{"changed":false},"itemTemplateQuestionUuids":{"changed":false},"questionType":"ListQuestion","referenceUuids":{"changed":false},"requiredPhaseUuid":{"changed":false},"tagUuids":{"changed":true,"value":["4fa6f10d-b593-4b00-84cf-00d7f916147f"]},"text":{"changed":true,"value":"Processing of certain categories of personal data is not allowed unless there are exemptions in law to allow this. Among these categories (“sensitive data”) are *“‘[...] data revealing racial or ethnic origin, [...] genetic data, [...] data concerning health’”*. Most types of personal data collected in biomedical research will fall under these categories. [Article 9](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-9-gdpr/) (2) lists a number of exemptions that apply, of which *consent* and *scientific research* are most likely to be relevant for research. Please consult with your Data Protection Officer of your organisation."},"title":{"changed":true,"value":"What are the exemptions for the prohibition for processing of special categories of data (such as health and genetic data) under Art. 9 GDPR used? State cohort/dataset for each type of exemption."}},"createdAt":"2022-02-28T14:44:09Z","entityUuid":"de72effc-807a-4081-b842-1e77ecc9c43f","parentUuid":"7dd7320e-41dd-43b9-b6aa-7622eaa34679","uuid":"e621d239-4b9e-4458-b12a-9afe8acc788e"},{"content":{"annotations":[],"eventType":"AddQuestionEvent","questionType":"OptionsQuestion","requiredPhaseUuid":null,"tagUuids":[],"text":null,"title":""},"createdAt":"2022-02-28T14:44:10Z","entityUuid":"2418a1b7-6950-4a19-8e58-6c5089c71b53","parentUuid":"de72effc